All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: added `.lower()` to both sides of the role comparison so it matches case-insensitively (`auth.py:10`).
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` so that either admin status or ownership grants access (`auth.py:15`).

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: replaced mutable default argument `{}` with `None` and copied the input dict to avoid shared state between instances (`inventory.py:13`).
- `add`: changed from assignment (`=`) to accumulation (`+=`) so repeated adds stack (`inventory.py:20`).
- `reserve`: changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed (`inventory.py:28`).
- `release`: added a guard so releasing more than is currently reserved raises `ValueError` instead of going negative (`inventory.py:35`).

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: lowercased alphanumeric characters (`text_utils.py:19`) and replaced repeated `--` collapsing with a `while` loop so multiple consecutive separators fully collapse (`text_utils.py:23-24`).
- `truncate`: accounted for suffix length in the slice so total output length never exceeds `max_len` (`text_utils.py:33`).
